ain, oxidizes it to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde without molecular oxygen, applies a Strecker reaction to give histidine nitrile, and hydrolyzes the nitrile to histidine. The least secure step is the homologation of 4(5)-methylimidazole; the ten listed pathways arise from branching at the triose-to-methylglyoxal and imidazole-formation stages while keeping the rest of the chemistry shared.", "molecules": [{"id": "mol_001", "formula": "CH2O", "iupac_name": "methanal", "common_name": "formaldehyde", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_002", "formula": "C2H4O2", "iupac_name": "2-hydroxyethanal", "common_name": "glycolaldehyde", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_003", "formula": "C3H6O3", "iupac_name": "2,3-dihydroxypropanal", "common_name": "glyceraldehyde", "inchi": null, "role": "hub_intermediate", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_004", "formula": "C3H6O3", "iupac_name": "1,3-dihydroxypropan-2-one", "common_name": "dihydroxyacetone", "inchi": null, "role": "hub_intermediate", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_005", "formula": "C3H4O2", "iupac_name": "2-oxopropanal", "common_name": "methylglyoxal", "inchi": null, "role": "hub_intermediate", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_006", "formula": "NH3", "iupac_name": "azane", "common_name": "ammonia", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_007", "formula": "HCN", "iupac_name": "hydrogen cyanide", "common_name": "hydrogen cyanide", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_008", "formula": "CH3NO", "iupac_name": "methanamide", "common_name": "formamide", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_009", "formula": "C4H6N2", "iupac_name": "4-methyl-1H-imidazole", "common_name": "4(5)-methylimidazole", "inchi": null, "role": "hub_intermediate", "environment_formed": "Surface"}, {"id": "mol_010", "formula": "C5H8N2O", 