s)\n  - P3: Glyceraldehyde surface oxidation plus clay Debus route (7 steps)\n  - P4: Glyceraldehyde hydrothermal oxidation plus aqueous Debus route (7 steps)\n  - P5: Glyceraldehyde hydrothermal oxidation plus formamide Debus route (7 steps)\n  - P6: Glyceraldehyde hydrothermal oxidation plus clay Debus route (7 steps)\n  - P7: Dihydroxyacetone surface conversion plus aqueous Debus route (7 steps)\n  - P8: Dihydroxyacetone surface conversion plus formamide Debus route (7 steps)\n  - P9: Dihydroxyacetone hydrothermal conversion plus aqueous Debus route (7 steps)\n  - P10: Dihydroxyacetone hydrothermal conversion plus clay Debus route (7 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 12 reactions | 1 balanced as written | 1 balanceable with coefficients | 10 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 balanceable: 2 CH2O + 2 C2H4O2 -> C3H6O3 + C3H6O3\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: C3H6O3 -> C3H4O2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: C3H6O3 -> C3H4O2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: C3H6O3 -> C3H4O2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: C3H6O3 -> C3H4O2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: C3H4O2 + CH2O + NH3 -> C4H6N2 | reactants minus products: H+3, N-1, O+3 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: C3H4O2 + CH2O + CH3NO -> C4H6N2 | reactants minus products: C+1, H+3, N-1, O+4 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_008 UNBALANCED: C3H4O2 + CH2O + NH3 -> C4H6N2 | reactants minus products: H+3, N-1, O