sent, the step installs the histidine alpha-amino nitrile skeleton in one balanced transformation."}, {"id": "rxn_011", "name": "Hydrolysis of histidine nitrile to histidine", "inputs": ["mol_013", "mol_010"], "outputs": ["mol_014", "mol_008"], "environment": "Biochemical", "agents": null, "conditions": {"temperature": "330-370K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": "true", "other": "warm aqueous geothermal cycling; prolonged residence times; anoxic"}, "mechanism": "Stepwise nitrile hydration to the amide and then to the carboxylic acid with ammonia release.", "reasoning": "Aminonitriles hydrolyze to amino acids in warm water over geologically relevant timescales. Explicit water consumption and ammonia release keep the final step fully balanced and chemically transparent."}, {"id": "rxn_012", "name": "Erythrulose to erythrose isomerization", "inputs": ["mol_006"], "outputs": ["mol_005"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": ["borate minerals"], "conditions": {"temperature": "300-340K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": "borate minerals", "aqueous": "true", "other": "carbonyl equilibration in partially evaporating pools; anoxic"}, "mechanism": "Reverse enediol-mediated aldose-ketose isomerization.", "reasoning": "Because erythrose and erythrulose should interconvert in the same surface network, the reverse direction is included explicitly so the directed graph can represent oxo-dialdehyde access through either tetrose isomer without violating stoichiometry."}], "pathways": [{"pathway_id": "P1", "name": "Glycolaldehyde dimer route with surface imidazole closure", "description": "Glycolaldehyde dimerizes to erythrose, hydrothermal redox-dehydration gives the oxo-dialdehyde, surface Debus condensation forms imidazole-4-acetaldehyde, and the common Strecker-hydrolysis sequence yields histidine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_004", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_010", "rxn_011"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_005", "mol_007", "mol_012", "mol_013"]}, {"pathway_id": "P2"