ns\": [\"rxn_011\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_012\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}", "parsed_response": {"target_molecule": "Histidine", "overall_strategy": "Histidine is approached through its direct Strecker precursor, imidazole-4-acetaldehyde. The network first assembles the side-chain-bearing alpha-keto dialdehyde 2-oxobutane-1,4-dial from simple C1/C2 feedstocks: formaldehyde is generated hydrothermally from CO2, glycolaldehyde is reached either by surface formose chemistry or hydrothermal hydrogenation of glyoxal, acetaldehyde comes from glycolaldehyde deoxygenation or acetylene hydration, and glyoxal plus acetaldehyde undergo aldol addition followed by dehydrogenation. Debus-Radziszewski cyclization of 2-oxobutane-1,4-dial with formaldehyde and ammonia gives imidazole-4-acetaldehyde directly, avoiding weak post-ring homologation of simpler imidazoles, and Strecker formation followed by nitrile hydrolysis yields histidine. Small mobile C1/C2 feedstocks can transfer between settings more plausibly than the unstable C4 dialdehydes, and H2O, H2, and NH3 are included explicitly so the network is mass- and redox-balanced.", "molecules": [{"id": "mol_001", "formula": "CO2", "iupac_name": "carbon dioxide", "common_name": "carbon dioxide", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_002", "formula": "H2", "iupac_name": "dihydrogen", "common_name": "hydrogen", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_003", "formula": "CH2O", "iupac_name": "methanal", "common_name": "formaldehyde", "inchi": null, "role": "hub_intermediate", "environment_formed": "Hydrothermal"}, {"id": "mol_004", "formula": "C2H4O2", "iupac_name": "2-hydroxyethanal", "common_name": "glycolaldehyde", "inchi": null, "role": "hub_intermediate", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_005", "formula": "C2H2O2", "iupac_name": "ethanedial", "common_name": "glyoxal", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_006